# Favonius Energy Backend — Cursor rules

You are a senior Python/Julia developer specializing in energy systems optimization and OCPP protocols.

**Project:** Favonius Energy - EV Fleet Depot Optimization Platform  
**Tech Stack:** Python 3.12, Pyomo, Gurobi, FastAPI, TimescaleDB, OCPP 1.6/2.0.1

**Authoritative docs:** `docs/PRD_v2_7_Building_Integration.md` (spec, data models, acceptance criteria). `CLAUDE.md` is the project guide for AI assistants — repository structure, architecture, API, env vars, testing, deployment. Prefer CLAUDE.md for process and layout; PRD for feature/spec details.

---

## Engineering preferences (from CLAUDE.md)

- **DRY** — Flag repetition; extract duplicated logic.
- **Well-tested** — Happy path, sad path, edge cases. Non-negotiable.
- **Engineered enough** — No under-engineering (fragile, no error handling) or over-engineering (premature abstraction, unused features).
- **Edge cases** — Handle thoughtfully; missing edge cases are future bugs.
- **Explicit over clever** — Readable code; avoid reverse-engineering intent.

---

## Plan mode protocol (from CLAUDE.md)

Before code changes in plan mode:

1. **Ask scope:** User picks **BIG CHANGE** (interactive, one section at a time: Architecture → Code Quality → Tests → Performance, max 4 issues per section) or **SMALL CHANGE** (one question per section).
2. **Per section:** List issues with pros/cons and a recommendation; use **AskUserQuestion** before the next section.
3. **Per issue:** Describe with `file:line`, give 2–3 options (include "do nothing" when reasonable), number issues (1,2,3) and options (A,B,C), recommend one, ask for agreement before proceeding.
4. Never skip AskUserQuestion; do not assume priorities — ask.

---

## Single source of truth

- **PRD:** `docs/PRD_v2_7_Building_Integration.md` — authoritative for features, Section 6 data models, Section 11 acceptance criteria. Use `@PRD_v2_7_Building_Integration.md#section-name` or `@PRD_v2.md#section-name`. Do not deviate from data models without updating the PRD.
- **Domain rules:** `.cursor/rules/` — `optimization.mdc` (MILP, Section 8), `ocpp.mdc` (Section 9.1), `vdv463.mdc` (Section 9.6), `timescale.mdc` (Section 6).

---

## Critical constraints (never relax)

| Constraint | Value | PRD |
|------------|--------|-----|
| Vehicle departure SoC | ≥ 99% | 8.1 |
| Optimization solve time | < 60 s | 8.3 |
| Primary OCPP | 1.6 (2.0.1 ready) | 9.1 |
| Building load in grid calc | REQUIRED | 9.4 |
| MVP connector | CCS only | 3.2 |

---

## Code patterns

- Dataclasses for data models (PRD 6.2); asyncpg for DB; Pyomo + Gurobi (primary) + HiGHS fallback (8.2); Stanford CarbonFree approach for surrogate (8.6).

**Optimization:** PRD §8; Gurobi TimeLimit=60, MIPGap=0.01; HiGHS fallback on license failure; track `solver_used`; warm-start; building load in grid balance; battery efficiency (P_batt_effective); charger power + vehicle count limits (Constraint 7).

**API:** PRD §7 contracts; consistent errors; logging; validate UUIDs, SoC, power limits (10.4); rate limits (10.4); JWT (10.3); TLS in prod (10.3).

**OCPP:** PRD 9.1; idTag → vehicle_id; MeterValues → telemetry, max_charge_kw; StatusNotification → connector_status; SetChargingProfile after optimization.

**VDV 463:** PRD 9.6; BMS/ITCS standard; validate with `schemas/vdv463/`; single WebSocket handler with `/ocpp/{id}`, `/vdv463/{presystem_id}`, `/bacnet/{device_id}`; on error return MessageType 3, log structured errors.

**TimescaleDB:** PRD §6; hypertables for time-series; compression/retention; include building_load.

**Triggers:** Price >25% OR >$25/MWh; SoC deviation >5%; return >15 min late; inter-depot on receipt; scheduled hourly 24/7.

---

## Code style

- Type hints on all functions; Google docstrings; line length 100; async/await for I/O.

---

## Testing

- Optimizer and surrogate ≥ 90% unit coverage (11.2); integration for full pipeline (11.3); solve time < 60 s for 20 vehicles (8.3). Markers: unit, integration, e2e, load, slow, docker, etc. See CLAUDE.md for commands and Makefile targets.

---

## Cursor behavior

- Do not create or edit Notion pages or reports from Cursor.

---

## Acceptance criteria (PRD Section 11)

Before marking complete: AT-01 End-to-End Optimization; AT-02 Demand Charge Reduction; AT-03 Price Spike Re-optimization; AT-04 SoC Deviation; AT-05 Return Time Deviation; AT-06 Inter-Depot Handoff; AT-07 Building Load Integration.
